<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manchuria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manchuria is a region of north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. It was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchus</a>, who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> and conquered China from there. In the twentieth century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> occupied Manchuria, and earlier steppe empires such as the Gokturks extended their influence into it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manchuria.jpg" alt="Manchuria" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CIA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manchuria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
